{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27147194","formula":"C₁₅H₁₅NO₂S","hill":"C15H15NO2S","elements":["H","C","N","O","S"],"composition":{"C":15.0,"H":15.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"(S)-modafinil"},"descriptions":{"en":"Esmodafinil (also known as (S)-modafinil or (+)-modafinil; developmental code name CRL-40983) is the enantiopure (S)-(+)-enantiomer of modafinil. Unlike armodafinil ((R)-(−)-modafinil), esmodafinil has never been marketed on its own. Esmodafinil is suspected to be less clinically useful for treating conditions that modafinil and armodafinil are marketed for, such as narcolepsy, shift work sleep disorder, and obstructive sleep apnea."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":11173366,"mass":273.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C(C=C1)C(C2=CC=CC=C2)[S@@](=O)CC(=O)N","inchikey":"YFGHCGITMMYXAQ-IBGZPJMESA-N","iupac":"2-[(S)-benzhydrylsulfinyl]acetamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11173366","atoms":34,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.95,"y":-1.329,"z":-0.448,"el":"S"},{"x":-0.659,"y":-2.705,"z":0.039,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.013,"y":-1.411,"z":-1.23,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.318,"y":-2.098,"z":0.942,"el":"N"},{"x":0.227,"y":-0.212,"z":0.442,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.071,"y":1.236,"z":0.245,"el":"C"},{"x":1.68,"y":-0.597,"z":0.167,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.409,"y":-0.717,"z":0.422,"el":"C"},{"x":0.076,"y":2.129,"z":1.306,"el":"C"},{"x":2.416,"y":-1.168,"z":1.181,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.496,"y":1.698,"z":-1.001,"el":"C"},{"x":2.201,"y":-0.358,"z":-1.085,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.202,"y":3.483,"z":1.123,"el":"C"},{"x":3.742,"y":-1.52,"z":0.929,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.774,"y":3.052,"z":-1.185,"el":"C"},{"x":3.528,"y":-0.71,"z":-1.337,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.627,"y":3.945,"z":-0.123,"el":"C"},{"x":4.298,"y":-1.29,"z":-0.329,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.648,"y":-1.429,"z":-0.057,"el":"C"},{"x":0.025,"y":-0.443,"z":1.49